  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 cup erythritol (powdered)",
    "1/2 cup blackberries (strained)",
    "2 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "6 tablespoon butter (softened)",
    "1/4 cup heavy whipping cream",
    "1/3 cup butter (salted)",
    "1/4 cup erythritol (powdered)",
    "1 1/2 cup almond flour",
    "2 tablespoon psyllium husk powder",
    "2 tablespoon poppy seeds",
    "1 1/2 teaspoon baking powder",
    "2 large egg",
    "1/2 cup sour cream",
    "2 teaspoon lemon zest",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1/4 teaspoon liquid stevia"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Start by putting the butter for the cake into a pan over medium heat. Preheat oven to 350F.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1304.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grind erythritol for the cake in a spice grinder until powdered completely. Let settle before removing lid.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1320.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add almond flour, powdered erythritol, psyllium husk powder, poppy seeds and baking powder into a bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1325.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate bowl, mix together eggs, sour cream, lemon zest, vanilla extract and liquid stevia.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1328.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keep an eye on your butter until it browns; it should look a deep golden color.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1331.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly pour the browned butter into the wet ingredients while mixing with your spoon.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1340.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add dry ingredients a little bit at a time while mixing until your batter forms.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1351.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grease a round cake pan, then press your batter into the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1354.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20-25 minutes, until the cake is golden brown on the top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1355.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let the cake cool slightly, then remove from the pan and let cool on a cooling rack.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1368.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grind remaining erythritol in a spice grinder, then grind blackberries until a paste is formed (you can use a food processor for this, or your spice grinder if you immediately clean it out). Strain the paste into a separate container, making sure no seeds get through.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1381.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add lemon juice and powdered erythritol to the blackberry puree and mix together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1391.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate bowl (or clean out one of the bowls you used earlier), beat together remaining butter with heavy cream using a hand mixer.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1402.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly mix in the blackberry puree until a thick icing is formed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1408.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Plop the icing on the cake and cover the entire cake, sides included.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1410.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place in the refrigerator for 20-30 minutes, then serve!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/lemon-poppy-seed-cake-with-blackberry-buttercream/#wprm-recipe-51285-step-0-15",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
